Installation Instructions for PySplot.

Download the zip file and unzip.
https://github.com/thomasjoshd/pysplot/archive/refs/heads/master.zip

Folder structure is something like:
downloaded_location/pysplot-master/

I created a folder called pysplotenv in the downloaded_location/, to hold my
python environment.

From downloaded_location/ Get a python3 environment going (if you wish).
mkdir pysplotenv
python3 -m venv pysplotenv
source pysplotenv/bin/activate

Then navigate to the pysplot-master/ folder.
If you are on linux/mac you can run: bash pysplot-master/setup.sh

Otherwise to get the necessary libraries,
 run the following command in the directory you installed to.

pip install --upgrade pip
pip install --upgrade -r requirements.txt

or

pip3 install --upgrade pip
pip3 install --upgrade -r requirements.txt


Running PySplot from pysplot-master/ folder.
If you are on linux/mac you can run: bash pysplot.sh

Otherwise run PySplot from the commandline: python3 PySplot/PySplot.py

Enjoy!
